<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94479" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάζω</span></b> , only pres. and
		impf., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>limp,
			halt</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.811
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
				610
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.317e
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκέσασθαι τὸ
			σκάζον</span> make good <i>the damage</i>, Men.Prot.<i><span class="en">
				p.22
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρῶ τὰ ἡμέτερα
			σκάζοντα</span>, of parasites, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.50
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἀμφοτέροις ἡ κρίσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chor.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				49.504
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὴν θεραπείαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
					39
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάζων, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντος</span>,
					ὁ</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χωλίαμβος</span>, the iambic verse of Hipponax, with a
			spondee in the last place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάζοντα μέτρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.405
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>). (Cf. Skt. <i>kháñjati</i> 'limp', <i><span class="en">
				Germ.
			</span></i>
			<i>hinken.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
